# VoiceThing Style System

## Structure
```
styles/
├── __init__.py      # get_style("macos_2005") returns style instance
├── base.py          # BaseStyle with defaults - override what you need
└── macos_2005.py    # Mid-2000s macOS Aqua brushed metal
```

## Adding a new style

1. Create `styles/windows_95.py`:
```python
from .base import BaseStyle

class Windows95Style(BaseStyle):
    name = "windows_95"
    font = "MS Sans Serif"
    # Override colors, CSS methods, etc.
```

2. Register in `styles/__init__.py`:
```python
STYLES = {"macos_2005": MacOS2005Style, "windows_95": Windows95Style}
```

3. Use: `STYLE = get_style("windows_95")` in voice_thing.py
